   terms of the GNU Affero General Public License as published by the Free Software
   Foundation, either version 3 of the License, or (at your option) any later version.
   It is distributed in the hope that it will be useful, but WITHOUT ANY WARRANTY; without
   even the implied warranty of MERCHANTABILITY or FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE. The
   full text of the licence is in COPYING.

   Additional terms, as section 7 of the licence permits them ((b), (c) and (e)):

   (b) A modified version must keep the attribution "History Globe by Vadym Arnaut",
       with a link to https://historyglobe.app, in the notice or "about" information it
       shows its users (in the original: the Author and Build pages of the Help).
   (c) A modified version must be marked as different from the original: it may not
       present itself as History Globe, or as made or endorsed by its author.
   (e) The licence grants no right under trademark law to use the name "History Globe"
       or its logo (part 6).
   Under (c) and (e) together, a modified version that users interact with goes under a
   name of its own.

   Two exceptions, so that the parts meant to run inside other sites can be used there
   freely:

   - The places-in-any-text script, apps/web/public/hg-places.js and its released
     versions apps/web/public/hg-places-*.js, is under the MIT licence:
     https://opensource.org/license/mit
   - The code examples in content/docs/ (the embedding snippets and the API examples) are
     dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0:
     https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/

2. The articles and the questions: CC BY-NC-ND 4.0

   The place articles (content/articles/), the questions and their answers
   (content/questions/), in every language they are written or translated in, and the
   files the build makes of them (apps/web/public/data/articles/, the article text on the
   place pages, the question pages, api/v1/questions.json) are licensed under the
   Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-NoDerivatives 4.0 International licence:
   https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/

   In short (the licence's own text governs): you may copy and share them unchanged,
   in any medium or format, with credit and not for commercial purposes, on another
   site or in a collection too. You may not share a changed or translated version of
   them. Short quotations with credit, as the law allows them, and links need no
   licence. Credit: "History Globe (Vadym Arnaut), CC BY-NC-ND 4.0", with a link to
   the page.

   Until 2026-10-17 these texts were offered under CC BY 4.0. Copies made under that
   licence keep it (a Creative Commons licence cannot be revoked); what is published
   from that date on is under this one.

   Text and data mining. The copyright holder expressly reserves the right to reproduce
   and extract these texts for text and data mining, within the meaning of Article 4(3)
   of Directive (EU) 2019/790, including for the training, fine-tuning or evaluation of
   machine-learning models. The reservation covers this part only. Its machine-readable
   form is the robots.txt of historyglobe.app (the Disallow lines for training crawlers
   and the Content-Signal line, "ai-train=no") and the "tdm-reservation: 1" header the
   site sends with every page.

3. The data: CC BY 4.0

   - The curated content in content/ other than articles/, questions/, docs/, reviews/
     and drafts/: place names in every language, tours, events, battles, when towns stood,
     ancient-author notes, photo records and the rest;
   - the data the build makes from it: apps/web/public/data/ except articles/, photos/
     and verses/, and the open API in apps/web/public/api/ except questions.json;
   - the data files kept beside the code: pipeline/rivers/rivers.geojson (derived from
     RiverATLAS, CC BY 4.0), pipeline/rivers/targets.json,
     pipeline/ancient/names-cyrillic.json, pipeline/dataset_card.md, and the crosswalk
     tables docs/crosswalk/*.csv

   are licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International licence:
   https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

   Credit: "History Globe (Vadym Arnaut), CC BY 4.0", with a link to the source where
   the medium allows.

   The theographic_* columns of docs/crosswalk/places.csv hold the record ids of
   Theographic Bible Metadata (CC BY-SA 4.0) and a few values quoted as evidence; they
   are cited, not licensed here. content/drafts/ holds Wikidata labels (CC0) and stays
   under CC0.

   Not licensed here: apps/web/public/data/photos/ holds Wikimedia Commons photographs,
   each under the licence its record names (content/photos.yaml; the place card and the
   place page show it), and apps/web/public/data/verses/ holds the Bible text of
   public-domain editions (docs/ATTRIBUTIONS.md, "Scripture").

4. The reviews

   The reviews in content/reviews/ belong to their authors. Each file names its author
   and the licence the author gave it (the "licence" field).

5. Third-party data, images and software

   Third-party data, images and software included or referenced here remain under their
   own licences (OpenBible.info, STEPBible TIPNR, Cliopatria, Pleiades, Itiner-e,
   RiverATLAS, Natural Earth, Copernicus WorldDEM-30 and the other elevation models,
   Wikimedia Commons photographs, the public-domain Bible editions, MapLibre, React,
   Lucide, the fonts and others); see docs/ATTRIBUTIONS.md and apps/web/public/licenses/.
   The grants in parts 1 to 3 and the reservation in part 6 cover this project's own
   contribution only; they relicense and reserve none of these.

6. The name and the logo: not licensed

   The name "History Globe" and its logo (apps/web/public/favicon.*, icon-*.png,
   apple-touch-icon.png) are not licensed under any of the above. All rights reserved.

   The preview images (apps/web/public/og.jpg, og/, shots/) are pictures of the site.
   The project's own part of them, its interface with the name and the logo, is not
   licensed either. What they show of the data and the texts keeps the licence of its
   part above, and what they show from third parties keeps its own licence (part 5):
   the borders from Cliopatria (CC BY 4.0), the relief from Copernicus WorldDEM-30 and
   the other elevation models, Natural Earth, and the photographs in the place card,
   each under the licence printed on it (in shots/*-place.jpg, Jerusalem by Kok Leng
   Yeo, CC BY 2.0).
